/P 74 0 R
/E (L1 cache is located closest to the CPU core and provides the fastest access. It stores frequently used instructions and data. L2 cache has greater capacity but slightly higher latency. L3 cache is larger and is often shared between processor cores. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [19]
>>
endobj
188 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 74 0 R
/E (A higher cache hit rate means the processor can obtain data without accessing slower main memory. Therefore, L1 has the greatest effect on reducing latency, while L2 and L3 help reduce the number of DRAM accesses. A well-designed cache hierarchy improves processor throughput and overall performance. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [20]
>>
endobj
