194 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 74 0 R
/E (The cache hierarchy improves processor performance by keeping frequently accessed information close to the CPU. When data is found in L1, the processor gets the lowest latency. If there is an L1 miss, L2 and then L3 are checked before accessing DRAM. Thus, increasing cache hit rates improves effective memory access time and processor throughput. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [26]
>>
